notes.body:
There are multiple indications a dissector might return:

- "I dissected N bytes worth of data";
- "This isn't a packet for my protocol";
- "This appears to be a packet for my protocol, but I need N more bytes from the lower layer" (for direction of protocols that are encapsulated in a byte-stream protocol such as TCP or TLS);
- "This appears to be a packet for my protocol, but I need the next segment from the lower layer";
- "This appers to be a packet for my protocol, but I need all of the remaining data up to the end of the connection";

and possibly others.  We might want to come up with a way to handle that.

